// ROB-21 corpus: the shader re-includes a stage-guarded header once in the
// shared region and again in the fragment region (the koko-aio pattern). The
// fragment translation unit therefore contains the header's sampler
// declaration twice; the translator must dedupe it to one dense binding
// (first binding wins) instead of emitting a glslang "redefinition" failure
// and double-counting num_samplers.
shader0 = shaders/dupinclude.slang
textures = "dup"
dup = "textures/lut.png"
